IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Fair Trading Act 1986 (New Zealand) — THE NOUNS.
--
-- Every fact the rule modules read, and nothing else: no rules, no #EVAL.
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_1986_121.txt (New Zealand
-- Legislation, version as at 1 July 2026, converted from the PCO XML).
-- Field names are unique across records.

§ `Fair Trading Act 1986 — the nouns`

§§ `Persons and days`

DECLARE `Kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a body corporate`

-- Working days: the weekdays that are not working days (public holidays and
-- the like) are an input; Saturdays and Sundays are never working days.
DECLARE `Working day calendar` HAS
    `weekdays that are not working days`                IS A LIST OF DATE

§§ `Conduct (Part 1, Parts 2-4A)`

-- The provisions a person may be said to contravene, one constructor each.
DECLARE Prohibition IS ONE OF
    `s 7 unconscionable conduct in trade`
    `s 9 misleading or deceptive conduct in trade`
    `s 10 conduct liable to mislead the public about goods`
    `s 11 conduct liable to mislead the public about services`
    `s 12 misleading conduct about employment`
    `s 12A an unsubstantiated representation in trade`
    `s 13 a false or misleading representation about goods or services`
    `s 14(1) a false or misleading representation about land`
    `s 14(2) force, harassment or coercion about land`
    `s 16 forging or falsely applying a trade mark`
    `s 17 offering gifts or prizes not intended to be provided`
    `s 19 bait advertising`
    `s 19(2) not offering advertised goods or services at the advertised price`
    `s 20 referral selling`
    `s 21 accepting payment without intending to supply`
    `s 21A(2) a trader sending unsolicited goods without telling the recipient their rights`
    `s 21C asserting a right to payment for unsolicited goods or services`
    `s 22 misleading representations about business activities`
    `s 23 harassment or coercion`
    `s 24 promoting or operating a pyramid selling scheme`
    `s 26A or 26B using an unfair contract term`
    `s 28 a consumer information standard`
    `s 28B disclosing trader status online`
    `s 30 a product safety standard`
    `s 31 supplying goods under an unsafe goods notice`
    `s 31A not notifying a voluntary recall`
    `s 32 a compulsory recall notice`
    `s 33D a suspension of supply notice`
    `s 36 a services safety standard`
    `s 36C or 36D layby disclosure`
    `s 36F a layby cancellation charge`
    `s 36L uninvited direct sale disclosure`
    `s 36RA entering or not leaving residential premises`
    `s 36U extended warranty disclosure`
    `s 36WB a gift card expiring in less than 3 years`
    `s 36WC a gift card without a prominent expiry`
    `s 36ZB, 36ZD or 36ZF auction duties`

-- s 5D(1), (3): a clause contracting out of ss 9, 12A, 13 or 14(1).
DECLARE `Contracting out clause` HAS
    `the agreement is in writing`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `supplied and acquired in trade`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `all parties are in trade`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `all parties agree to contract out`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is fair and reasonable that the parties are bound` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 15: publication or broadcast by news media.
DECLARE `News media facts` HAS
    `published in a newspaper or broadcast by the publisher or broadcaster` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an advertisement`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `about the publisher's or broadcaster's own supply, or a party's under an arrangement with it` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Conduct case` HAS
    `provision engaged`                                 IS A Prohibition
    -- the conduct, as found, has the quality the provision describes
    -- (misleading, unconscionable, unsubstantiated, false, and so on).
    `the conduct has the quality the provision describes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in trade`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `person`                                            IS A `Kind of person`
    `the person is the Crown`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `news media`                                        IS A MAYBE `News media facts`
    `clause contracting out`                            IS A MAYBE `Contracting out clause`
    -- s 12A(3): "a representation that a reasonable person would not expect
    -- to be substantiated"; s 12D: another enactment sets the grounds and
    -- the person complied with it.
    `a reasonable person would not expect substantiation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `complied with another enactment setting the grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 43A: when the loss or damage was discovered or ought reasonably to
    -- have been discovered.
    `loss discovered on`                                IS A DATE

§§ `Layby sales (ss 36B-36J)`

DECLARE `Layby facts` HAS
    `possession only once all or part of the price is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `instalments, counting any deposit`                 IS A NUMBER
    `the agreement says it is a layby sale agreement`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `purchase price`                                    IS A NUMBER
    -- s 36B(2) "or, if greater, the amount specified in section 10(1A)(b) of
    -- the Disputes Tribunal Act 1988".
    `the Disputes Tribunal Act amount`                  IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Who cancelled the layby` IS ONE OF
    `the consumer, before taking possession`
    `the supplier, for a breach of a material term by the consumer`
    `the supplier, the goods being unavailable with no satisfactory substitute`
    `the supplier, having ceased trading`

DECLARE `Layby cancellation` HAS
    `who cancelled`                                     IS A `Who cancelled the layby`
    `the agreement provides for a cancellation charge`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the supplier has breached the agreement`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `cancellation charge claimed`                       IS A NUMBER
    `the supplier's reasonable costs arising directly from the agreement` IS A NUMBER
    `paid under the agreement`                          IS A NUMBER

§§ `Uninvited direct sales and extended warranties (ss 36K-36W)`

DECLARE `Where the negotiations took place` IS ONE OF
    `in person at the consumer's home or workplace, uninvited`
    `by a telephone call the consumer did not invite`
    `elsewhere, or by invitation`

DECLARE `Direct sale facts` HAS
    `negotiations`                                      IS A `Where the negotiations took place`
    `price paid or payable`                             IS A NUMBER
    `the price cannot be ascertained at the time of supply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a renewal agreement`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `supplied in trade to a consumer`                   IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Auctions (ss 14A, 36X-36ZF)`

DECLARE `Vendor bid facts` HAS
    `the terms permit vendor bids`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the bid was identified as a vendor bid`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a reserve price`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the bid is below the reserve price`                IS A BOOLEAN
